Z||000000||count_iblis||09-29-2000||06:19 PM||||i dont know if any of you all remember this but as you were about 45 miles south of lousiville in kentucky the guy in a red probe gt went buying all of you all honking my horn and giving thumbs up to all the beautiful fieros, anyone remember this?  Any was that was me.  I wasnt able to see the show this year and i probably wont ever get a chance to see one agian unless it comes here again, just wanted to say it broguht a tear to my eye when I saw of you all driving down the interstate.  <P>Good bless the fiero<P><BR>Count<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Chris Schaefer||10-01-2000||09:55 AM||||Count,<P>I was in Louisville this year for the FOCOA Nationals.  I arrived on Thursday afternoon.  That afternoon we went to go visit my wife's Great Aunt.  She lives about 15 minutes south of the river.  The only other time I drove the car anywhere was to clean it and show it.  That Sunday we left to return to Connecticut about 10:00am.  We drove south to connect with I64 through Lexington, Charleston.  In Charleston we took I79N to I68E plus many more Interstates and roads before we returned to Connecticut.<P>I do not believe that I was one of the cars you saw but you never know.<P>It is too bad that you could not have made it to the Nationals, maybe next year.  The FOCOA will be going to Williamsburg, VA.  ||||reg||6
